        "2310.04378_rag::chunk_005"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasEvidenceText "LDMs generate images via denoising using reverse diffusion"^^xsd:string,
        "Latent Diffusion Model (LDM) in order to compress data and denoise them in a smaller latent space"^^xsd:string,
        "Training diffusion models in the latent space greatly reduces the computation costs compared to pixel-based models and speeds up the inference process; LDMs make it possible to generate high-resolution images on laptop GPUs."^^xsd:string,
        "and latent diffusion models ( Rombach et al. , 2022 )"^^xsd:string,
        "another category of diffusion models that generate samples in the latent feature space has been proposed"^^xsd:string,
        "the LDM loosely decomposes perceptual compression and semantic compression by first cutting out the pixel-level redundancy with autoencoder and then manipulating/generating semantic ideas with the diffusion process on the learnt latent."^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :diffusion_model,
        :entity,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:skos_definition "A generative model that applies the diffusion process in the latent space of an autoencoder to decompose perceptual and semantic compression."^^xsd:string ;
