    kg:textSpan "slow speed and required computational cost. Several methods have been developed to address these drawbacks. Training-free Denoising Diffusion Implicit Model (DDIM) [ 157 ] is one of the advancements designed to accelerate the sampling process. DDIM extends the DDPM by substituting the Markovian process with the non-Markovian one, resulting in a faster sampling procedure with negligible quality degradation. [ 176 , 177 ] propose a suitable initialization instead of a random Gaussian noise in the " .

