    kg:textSpan "observation x 0 data ( x 0 ) to a reference distribution x T q T ( x T ) , and a backward process, which is also Markovian, that recovers the data distribution from x T . Specically, the forward process is dened through simple corruption operations, q t +1 | t . For continuous data the corruption kernel usually adds Gaussian noise ( Ho et al. , 2020 ); whereas for discrete data, where x 0 X with nite cardinality |X| , the corruption kernel can be uniform, discrete Gaussian, or some other choice " .

