    kg:docId "2301.13362_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2301_13362_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "we can explore alternative paths for optimal solutions during online optimization. 1. Introduction Denoising diffusion probabilistic models (DDPMs) ( Ho et al. , 2020 ) are parameterized stochastic Markov chains with Gaussian noises, which are learned by gradually adding noises to the data as the forward process, computing the posterior as a backward process, and then training the DDPM to match the backward process. Advances in DDPM ( Nichol and Dhariwal , 2021 ; Dhariwal and Nichol , 2021 ) hav" .

