    kg:textSpan "can be divided into two categories: quantization-aware training (QAT) [ 16 , 38 , 24 , 70 , 66 ] and post-training quantization (PTQ) [ 35 , 44 , 22 , 62 , 36 ]. QAT involves simulating quantization during training to achieve good performance with lower precision, but it requires substantial time, computational resources, and access to the original dataset. In contrast, PTQ does not require fine-tuning and only needs a small amount of unlabeled data to calibrate. Recent studies have pushed the l" .

