    kg:textSpan "weight in Table 1. 3.2 Runge-Kutta-Based Multi-Step Alignment Distillation One of the key components of our CUD is catch-up sampling , which can be solved by different ODE solvers. Notably, Eulers method and Heuns method are the subsets of Runge-Kutta methods, w.r.t. , Runge-Kutta 12, and Runge-Kutta 23. So in this study, we apply Runge-Kutta methods to model catch-up sampling on a generic perspective. We only consider the RungeKutta algorithm up to order 3, as higher-order algorithms would lead" .

