    kg:textSpan "we propose a simple yet effective approach to improve likelihood-based GM s . Our method involves mollifying data using Gaussian noise, gradually reducing its variance, until recovering the original data distribution p data ( x ) . This mollification procedure is similar to the reverse process of diffusion models, where a prior noise distribution is smoothly transformed into the data distribution [ 69 , 25 , 70 ]. As already mentioned, data mollification alleviates the problem of manifold overfi" .

