    kg:textSpan "deviation of sampling trajectory and denoising trajectory (red curves) gradually increases from t = 80 to around t = 10 or t = 5 , respectively, and then quickly decreases until reaching their final samples. This implies that each initial sample may be affected by all possible modes with a large influence at first, and become intensely attracted by its unique mode after a turning point. This phenomenon also supports the strategy of placing time intervals densely near the minimum timestamp yet sp" .

