    kg:textSpan "change map. k t k is the value of the complement of the strength. Therefore, the values of the mask determine the last timestep where each region is overridden, controlling the amount of change of the region, due to the suffix principle . The masks are nested (Figure 2 ), therefore some regions are copied from the noised original image multiple times, in contrast to copying each region once according to its strength. Because the diffusion model has not been trained on intermediate images with ho" .

