    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2306_13078_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "Continuous Layout Editing of Single Images with Diffusion Models ZHIYUAN ZHANG , City University of Hong Kong, China ZHITONG HUANG , City University of Hong Kong, China JING LIAO , City University of Hong Kong, China arXiv:2306.13078v1 [cs.CV] 22 Jun 2023 Fig. 1. Our method can continuously edit the layout of a single image with multiple objects. The first column shows the input image, followed by three columns of edited results. The edited results preserve the visual properties of the input ima" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2306_13078_rag__chunk_001> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2306.13078_rag::chunk_001" ;
    kg:docId "2306.13078_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2306_13078_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "To address this gap, we propose the first framework for layout editing of a single image while preserving its visual properties, thus allowing for continuous editing on a single image. Our approach is achieved through two key modules. First, to preserve the characteristics of multiple objects within an image, we disentangle the concepts of different objects and embed them into separate textual tokens using a novel method called masked textual inversion. Next, we propose a training-free optimizat" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2306_13078_rag__chunk_002> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2306.13078_rag::chunk_002" ;
    kg:docId "2306.13078_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2306_13078_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "with any other region in the image. Our approach enables precise and flexible control over the positions of objects in the image, without requiring additional training or fine-tuning of the pre-trained diffusion model. Extensive experiments and perceptual studies have demonstrated that our proposed method is effective in editing the layout of single images and outperforms other baseline methods (modified to perform this task). We also provide a user interface for interactive layout editing to as" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2306_13078_rag__chunk_004> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2306.13078_rag::chunk_004" ;
    kg:docId "2306.13078_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2306_13078_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan ". 2022], a large-scale text-to-image model. Therefore, before discussing our method, we first introduce Latent Diffusion Models (LDMs) [Rombach et al . 2022], which is the theory of Stable Diffusion. LDMs consist of two key stages. In the first stage, the encoder of an autoencoder maps the image to latent space 0 = E( ) , and a decoder maps it back to image D(E( )) . In the second stage, a diffusion model is trained to denoise the noised latent = 0 + 1 , where is a factor to determine noise leve" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2306_13078_rag__chunk_009> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2306.13078_rag::chunk_009" ;
    kg:docId "2306.13078_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2306_13078_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "the textual inversion on the 4 EXPERIMENTS To evaluate our proposed method, we first compare it qualitatively and quantitatively with several baselines, and then conduct a user study to compare them perceptually. Additionally, we conduct several ablation studies to validate the effectiveness of each important component of our method and demonstrate its application in continuous layout editing, which was not feasible with previous methods. 6 Zhiyuan Zhang, Zhitong Huang, and Jing Liao (a) (b) (c)" .

