    kg:textSpan "image and then uses the updated tokens to fine-tune the crossattention layers of the model. The results show that if a single image contains multiple objects, the methods without a mask, including both Dreambooth and textual inversion, cannot precisely learn and disentangle the concepts of different objects, which may result in the loss of visual properties. For example, in Fig. 6, row 1, the shape and color of the flower change significantly in columns (c) and (d). Another issue with these meth" .

