    kg:textSpan "of denoising varies throughout the generation process. decision, it has to predict the output based on the current input and the information it has learned so far. Although it is confident enough for models to make early exiting decisions, there is always information loss without full layers [45]. To address this issue and retain as much information as possible, previous methods [39,45] utilize a simple layer-wise loss for every layer: a t h c a l { L } _{n } ^ t = \\sum _i^{N-1} \\lVert g_i(L_{i," .

