    kg:textSpan ") t 1 P t t ( e x t | h t ) + D t t ( e x t | h t ) , (2) 3 Gradient Flow DDIM DDIM Asyrp DDIM Figure 2. Left: One generation step of regular DDIM reverse process (solid line) and asymmetric DDIM reverse process (solid and dashed line). We take this one step as a unit for gradient checkpointing. Right: Conceptual illustration of our method. We generate x 0 from x T through DDIM reverse process. Starting from the same node ( e x T = x T ), we generate e x 0 through asymmetric DDIM reverse process" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2310_10647_rag__chunk_001> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2310.10647_rag::chunk_001" ;
    kg:docId "2310.10647_rag" ;
