    kg:textSpan "Section 3.2 . Lastly, utilizing gradient descent to improve the stability of the sampling process in Section 3.3 . 3.1. Noise Scheduler In the forward process, DDPM, DDIM and noise-based Cold Diffusion all rely on Equation ( 4 ) with the square root parameterization. This definition leads to two singularities at t = 0 and t = T ( dx t d ) and also causes more steps to be required in the reverse diffusion process. We propose changing the parameterization to: x t = cos( t ) x 0 + sin( t ) . where " .

