    kg:textSpan "to datasets that allow us to test strongly overparameterized models (compared to the dataset size), as well as models that are underparameterized. There is a subtlety in increasing the training data for VAEs: Since the goal of VAEs is to model p data ( x ), naive data augmentations might alter the target distribution if not carefully crafted. Hence, we ask the question: Can we have infinite training samples drawn from p data ( x ) ? The answer is likely to be No, unless we have access to the tru" .

