    kg:textSpan "Model as a p data ( x ). Figure 1 illustrates the intuition behind DMaaPx. The blue dots represent the finite data set D train . They are i.i.d. samples from the unknown underlying data distribution p data ( x ) which is shown by the dark-edged region. The green regions represent p DM ( x ). We use shaded areas (green), not dots, to highlight that p DM ( x ) models a continuous distribution which we can generate infinitely many samples from. Diffusion models for data types other than images are " .

