    :hasEvidenceText "CFG was proposed for improving the sample quality of conditional DMs. During CFG, the DM predicts denoised target of both positive condition ( e.g ., text prompt) and negative condition"^^xsd:string,
        "Classifier-free guidance [ 13 ] is a technique to guide the iterative sampling process of a DM towards a conditioning signal c"^^xsd:string,
        "Classifier-free guidance [ 13 ] is a technique to guide the iterative sampling process of a DM towards a conditioning signal c by mixing the"^^xsd:string,
        "Classifier-free guidance [ 13 ] is a technique to guide the iterative sampling process of a DM towards a conditioning signal c by mixing the p"^^xsd:string,
        "Ho and Salimans [ 28 ] introduce label-conditioned guidance that does not require a classifier. They obtain a combination of a conditional and unconditional network in a single model"^^xsd:string,
        "both CG and CFG require extra training with labeled data, which is not only time-consuming but also practically cumbersome"^^xsd:string,
        "classifier-free guidance strategy that achieves the similar effect as classifier guidance without the use of an additional classifier"^^xsd:string,
        "introduce label-conditioned guidance that does not require a classifier. They obtain a combination of a conditional and unconditional network in a single model"^^xsd:string,
        "our method can be applied together with CFG and further enhance its generation quality."^^xsd:string,
        "the guidance can be obtained by generative model itself without a classifier, termed 7 as classifier-free guidance"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :entity,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "Classifier-Free Guidance"^^xsd:string,
        "Classifier-free guidance"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A technique to guide the iterative sampling process of a diffusion model towards a conditioning signal by mixing conditional and unconditional outputs without an auxiliary classifier."^^xsd:string ;
