    kg:docId "2209.00796_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2209_00796_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "necessarily translate seamlessly to other modalities. Many important data domains have special structures that must be taken into account for diffusion models to function effectively. Difficulties may arise, for example, when models rely on score functions that are only defined on continuous data domains, or when data reside on low dimensional manifolds. To cope with these challenges, diffusion models have to be adapted in various ways. 5.1 Discrete Data Most diffusion models are geared towards " .

