    kg:textSpan "Samples During the classifier-guided reverse diffusion sampling process, there are two types of intermediate sample to be used for the classifier: the reverse-process sample b x t , and the predicted denoised sample: b x 0 ( t ) = ( b x t ( 1 t ) ( b x t , t )) / t (Song et al. [2020a], Bansal et al. [2023]). Considering off-the-shelf classifiers are typically not robust to Gaussian noise and not time-dependent, selecting the appropriate classifier input type is crucial to ensure the best fit. I" .

