    kg:textSpan "a forward noising process and a reverse denoising process. The forward process is a Gaussian transition, which gradually adds noise to the original image following a predefined noise scheduler. The final image is expected to follow standard Gaussian distribution. The reverse process progressively removes the noise from data sampled from standard Gaussian distribution to generate high-fidelity images. The backbone network is utilized to denoise from noised images. Formally, let x 0 be the sample " .

