    kg:textSpan "samples, before the recent rise of diffusion models [5]. GANs are also known as being difficult to train due to their adversarial objective [74], and often suffer from mode collapse. In contrast, diffusion models have a stable training process and provide more diversity because they are likelihoodbased. Despite these advantages, diffusion models are still inefficient when compared to GANs, requiring multiple network evaluations during inference. A key aspect for comparison between GANs and diffu" .

